1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,907
This bullet just went through a wall.

2
00:00:01,907 --> 00:00:03,179
The wall was fine.

3
00:00:03,179 --> 00:00:05,116
Games don't move objects smoothly.

4
00:00:05,116 --> 00:00:08,659
They jump them forward once per frame, then check for collisions.

5
00:00:08,659 --> 00:00:11,428
A slow object always lands touching the wall.

6
00:00:11,428 --> 00:00:13,443
But a fast bullet can be in front of the wall

7
00:00:13,443 --> 00:00:16,202
on one frame and already behind it on the next.

8
00:00:16,202 --> 00:00:19,139
The check never sees it touching. It's called tunnelling.

9
00:00:19,139 --> 00:00:22,017
The fix: sweep the bullet's whole path between frames

10
00:00:22,017 --> 00:00:23,447
and find where it would hit.

11
00:00:23,447 --> 00:00:26,062
Engines call it continuous collision detection.

12
00:00:26,062 --> 00:00:28,198
Follow: tomorrow, AI doesn't see letters.
